confirm.action_detect:
The AI image detection (SAM) searches this image for:

{terms}

What it finds goes into the list on the right, with a frame and a mask.

legend.info_2:
**Boxes** (the rectangle around an object): its **status**; untick one to fade those objects, with **All · None · Invert**.
- red: selected (it is saved or described when you choose so);
- blue: found, not selected;
- orange-yellow: a region that is already on Commons;
- green: a rectangle you drew yourself;
- grey, dashed: excluded;
- orange: just found by the latest search (not a status of its own);
- thicker: chosen in the list or under the mouse.

objects.search_info_2:
**Where it searches**:
- the name in the list (also when you changed it yourself with the pencil);
- the search term of the AI image detection;
- the Wikidata item (also its Q-number);
- your own caption;
- the AI's description.

original.info_1:
Each row is a proposal for 'depicts' (P180) on the original: a Wikidata item, with its image (P18) and description. Only what you tick goes along. Below it: where the proposal comes from, and how many objects on the image belong to it.
- **chosen by you for a cut-out**: the item from an object's Commons concept (already checked by you, so ticked);
- **AI search term**: a search term of the AI, looked up on Wikidata (not ticked; check first that it is the right item);
- **AI suggestion for a cut-out**: a suggestion from What is this?;
- **added by you**: an item you searched yourself.

panel.info_commons_1:
This shows what people have already recorded about this image on Commons. It comes before new AI suggestions:
- the captions;
- 'depicts' with a region (the yellow rectangles);
- 'depicts' without a region;
- the file notes.
